flowchart TD
    start([Design approved release scope]) --> inspect[Read the project concept and selected feature definitions]
%% @aidflow-context inspect
%% Load the approved concept, the exact approved scope, and only the feature
%% Definitions listed there. Do not design backlog items outside the scope.
%% @end-aidflow-context
    inspect --> integrate[Design the selected features as one coherent release]
%% @aidflow-context integrate
%% Design how the selected features work together as one version: shared
%% components, interfaces, dependencies, data flows, risks, rollout and test
%% approach. Trace every feature acceptance criterion to the integrated Design.

%% Record path: `docs/aidflow/releases/<version>/design.md`.
%% Record outline: Scope reference; Integrated approach; Components and interfaces; Data and end-to-end behavior; Feature-to-design traceability; Risks and tradeoffs; Rollout and test strategy.
%% Mutable statuses belong in the index. Example IDs and versions are placeholders.
%% @end-aidflow-context
    integrate --> review[Check architecture, interfaces, dependencies, risks and acceptance coverage]
    review --> quality{Design complete, consistent and acceptance criteria covered?}
    quality -- No: independently resolvable --> integrate
    quality -- Missing requirement or decision --> awaitingInput[Ask focused question and wait for user input]
    awaitingInput -- Sufficient answer received --> integrate
    quality -- Technical obstacle or unresolved conflict --> blocked([Blocked: report obstacle and unblock condition])
%% @aidflow-context awaitingInput
%% Follow the Question protocol in `reference/interaction.md` (relative to aidflow.md).
%% Save interaction awaiting-input, execution waiting-human, this node and the
%% caller stack. Do not return to the caller while waiting; partial answers stay
%% here. An answer does not approve requirements or scope changes: reconcile any
%% affected approved inputs through their owning phase before continuing Design.
%% @end-aidflow-context
    quality -- Yes: save reviewed draft --> designApproval{Integrated release design approved by user?}
%% @aidflow-context review
%% Inspect existing architecture and constraints. Check every acceptance criterion
%% has a design mapping and verification approach; check interfaces, dependencies,
%% failure paths, rollout and risks for contradictions or omissions. Correct
%% in-scope gaps autonomously before requesting approval. Do not invent product
%% requirements. Escalate unresolved decisions or lack of progress with evidence.
%% @end-aidflow-context
    designApproval -- No: revise and review again --> integrate
    designApproval -- Yes: save release design --> designReady([Release design approved])
%% @aidflow-context designApproval
%% The human approves the integrated Design against the current scope digest.
%% Bind approval to the exact Design digest and record evidence in `.aidflow/index.md`.
%% Material scope/design changes invalidate affected approvals using Project impact rules.

%% Release transition `scope-approved -> design-pending-approval`: Self-reviewed Design covers every scoped feature and records its scope digest; record_status becomes pending-approval. Owner: AI prepares and requests approval.

%% Release transition `design-pending-approval -> design-approved`: Design digest is explicitly approved; append approval event. Owner: Human.
%% @end-aidflow-context
    designApproval -- Defer release --> designDeferred([Release deferred])
    designApproval -- Cancel release --> designCancelled([Release cancelled])

    classDef boundary fill:#0b7fae,color:#ffffff,stroke:#0b7fae
    classDef approval fill:#fff0e8,color:#633b2c,stroke:#c68162
    class start,designReady,designDeferred,designCancelled,blocked boundary
    class designApproval approval
